# How Does This Connect to Federated Learning?

Now this is critical.

The paper you referenced:

> DRFL: Federated Learning for Diabetic Retinopathy

Federated learning simulates:

* Multiple hospitals
* Each hospital has its own DR data
* Data never leaves hospital
* Models are aggregated centrally

---

## Why Federated Learning Is Harder

In federated setup:

* Each client has non-IID data
* Some clients may have mostly class 0
* Some may lack class 3 entirely
* Imbalance becomes worse per client

So problems we observed centrally:

* Imbalance
* Class confusion
* Model bias

These become amplified in federated learning.

