# How Federated Learning Will Change Things

In federated learning:

1. Split dataset into K clients
2. Each client trains locally
3. Server aggregates weights (FedAvg)

Core problem:

[
w_{global} = \sum_{k=1}^{K} \frac{n_k}{N} w_k
]

Where:

* ( w_k ) = client model
* ( n_k ) = client data size

If data distribution differs per client:

* Aggregation may bias toward dominant distributions
* Minority class learning may degrade

---

# Why Paper Uses Advanced Aggregation

Many DRFL papers use:

* Median aggregation
* Robust aggregation
* Weighted averaging
* Personalized FL

Because simple FedAvg:

* Amplifies imbalance
* Fails under non-IID

